IMPORT prelude

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore) -- what the Act asks of a company and its directors at four steps in a company's life:
-- incorporation of a private company (ss 17(2), 17(5), 18(1), 19(1)-(4), 20, 22(1)-(2), 145(1)-(2), 146(1)-(1A), 171(1E),
-- 171(4A)); a share issue to an investor (ss 161, 63(1)-(3)); the investor's holding as a substantial shareholding (ss 79(2),
-- 81-84) and as a significant interest (Part 11A: ss 386AB, 386AC, 386AF(1A), (7)-(9), (12), Sixteenth Schedule paras 1-3);
-- a selective buy-back of another member's shares (ss 76B(1), (3), (5), (7), (8), 76D(2), (2A), (3), (4), (4A), (7), 76F(1)-(4),
-- with s 184(1) for the special resolution); and the incorporation of a company limited by guarantee (ss 17(5), 22(1)(c), (e),
-- 22(1AA), (1AB), 38(1)). The directors' general duty in s 157(1)-(3) runs through all four.
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation (version in force from 6 May 2026 to 20 October 2026), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/CoA1967.txt. The arrangement table at the head of the deposit is out of step with the body (it
-- lists s 161 as "Loans and quasi-loans to directors"); every section number here was read from the BODY, where s 161 is
-- "Approval of company required for issue of shares by directors".
--
-- WHY. Added on 12 October 2026 for REQ-0284 (Haziq scenario, event h042): "A person incorporates a private company, allots
-- shares to an investor who then holds 25%, later buys back a 20% holder's shares, and later still incorporates a company
-- limited by guarantee. What does each step require of the directors?"
--
-- NOT ENCODED: the prescribed forms, fees and documents (all left to regulations); the Registrar's powers under s 12(5); the
-- appeal under s 20(3); public companies' allotment returns (s 63A) and buy-back lodgments (s 76B(9)); the equal-access scheme
-- (s 76C), contingent purchase contracts (s 76DA) and market acquisitions (s 76E); treasury shares (ss 76H-76K) beyond the
-- fact that a share held in treasury is not cancelled; s 76G (reduction of capital or profits on cancellation); short-notice
-- special resolutions (s 184(2)) and written resolutions (ss 184A-184G) beyond s 76D(4A)'s dispensing with inspection; the
-- s 386AFA "no registrable controller" note and the s 386AG investigation notices; the Fourteenth Schedule list; the
-- registers of members (s 196A) and of substantial shareholders (s 88); ss 157A-157C; and the rest of the Act. The terms
-- "private company" and "public company" are restated here from ss 4(1) and 18(1) rather than imported from coa-definitions.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table, no
-- independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Companies Act 1967 -- formation, share issue, controllers, buy-back and the guarantee company`

§§ `17, 18, 19, 20, 22, 145, 146 -- incorporating a company`

-- s 17(2): "A company may be -- (a) a company limited by shares; (b) a company limited by guarantee; or (c) an unlimited
-- company."
DECLARE CompanyKind IS ONE OF
    `limited by shares`
    `limited by guarantee`
    `unlimited`

-- s 19(2): "Either -- (a) a registered qualified individual engaged in the formation of the proposed company; or (b) a person
-- named in the constitution as a director or the secretary of the proposed company, must make a declaration to the Registrar
-- that -- (c) all of the requirements of this Act relating to the formation of the company have been complied with; and (d)
-- he or she has verified the identities of the subscribers to the constitution, and of the persons named in the constitution
-- as officers of the proposed company".
DECLARE Declarant IS ONE OF
    `a registered qualified individual engaged in the formation`
    `a person named in the constitution as a director`
    `a person named in the constitution as the secretary`
    `nobody the Act names`

DECLARE Formation HAS
    `the kind of company` IS A CompanyKind
    `it is to have a share capital` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the constitution and prescribed documents were submitted` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the last day of the first financial year was furnished` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the prescribed fee was paid` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the section 19(2) declaration was made by` IS A Declarant
    `the declaration covers compliance and the verification of identities` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the constitution is dated and states its name, the members' liability and the subscribers` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the constitution states the guarantee up to a specified amount` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the constitution states the number of members it is registering with` IS A BOOLEAN
    `each subscriber declared the number of shares taken, not less than one` IS A BOOLEAN
    `named directors ordinarily resident in Singapore` IS A NUMBER
    `every named director is a natural person of 18 or over of full capacity` IS A BOOLEAN
    `every named director filed consent and the section 146(1A) statements before incorporation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the constitution restricts the right to transfer shares` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the constitution limits the members to not more than 50` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Registrar is satisfied of a section 20(2) ground` IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 19(1): "A person desiring the incorporation of a company must -- (a) submit to the Registrar the constitution of the
-- proposed company and such other documents as may be prescribed; (b) furnish the Registrar with the last day of the proposed
-- company's first financial year ...; and (c) pay the Registrar the prescribed fee."
-- The duty is the promoter's: before incorporation there are no directors.
GIVEN f IS A Formation
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 19(1) is complied with` f MEANS
        f's `the constitution and prescribed documents were submitted`
    AND f's `the last day of the first financial year was furnished`
    AND f's `the prescribed fee was paid`

GIVEN f IS A Formation
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 19(2) is complied with` f MEANS
        (NOT (f's `the section 19(2) declaration was made by` EQUALS `nobody the Act names`))
    AND f's `the declaration covers compliance and the verification of identities`

-- s 17(5): "As from 15 August 1984, no company limited by guarantee with a share capital may be registered under this Act."
GIVEN f IS A Formation
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 17(5) bars registration` f MEANS
        f's `the kind of company` EQUALS `limited by guarantee`
    AND f's `it is to have a share capital`

-- s 22(1): the constitution "must be dated and must state ... (a) the name of the company; (b) if ... limited by shares --
-- that the liability of the members is limited; (c) if ... limited by guarantee -- that the liability of the members is
-- limited and that each member undertakes to contribute ... such amount as may be required not exceeding a specified amount;
-- (d) if ... unlimited -- that the liability of the members is unlimited; (e) if the company is an unlimited company or a
-- company limited by guarantee -- the number of members with which the company is applying to be registered; (f) the full
-- names, addresses and occupations of the subscribers ...; and (g) that such subscribers are desirous of being formed into a
-- company ...".
-- s 22(2): "Each subscriber ... must, if the company is to have a share capital, make a declaration to the Registrar ... as to
-- the number of shares (not being less than one) that the subscriber agrees to take."
GIVEN f IS A Formation
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the constitution meets section 22` f MEANS
        f's `the constitution is dated and states its name, the members' liability and the subscribers`
    AND (    (NOT (f's `the kind of company` EQUALS `limited by guarantee`))
          OR f's `the constitution states the guarantee up to a specified amount`)
    AND (    f's `the kind of company` EQUALS `limited by shares`
          OR f's `the constitution states the number of members it is registering with`)
    AND (    (NOT f's `it is to have a share capital`)
          OR f's `each subscriber declared the number of shares taken, not less than one`)

-- s 145(1): "Every company must have at least one director who is ordinarily resident in Singapore ...".
-- s 145(2): "No person other than a natural person who has attained the age of 18 years and who is otherwise of full legal
-- capacity may be a director of a company."
-- s 146(1): "A person must not be named as a director or proposed director in -- (a) any document filed ... for the purposes
-- of the incorporation of a company ... unless, before -- (c) the incorporation of the company ... the person has complied with
-- the conditions set out in subsection (1A)": a declaration of consent to act, a statement of not being disqualified, and a
-- statement of not being debarred under s 155B (and, where there is a share qualification, the s 146(1A)(b) undertakings).
GIVEN f IS A Formation
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the named directors meet sections 145 and 146` f MEANS
        f's `named directors ordinarily resident in Singapore` AT LEAST 1
    AND f's `every named director is a natural person of 18 or over of full capacity`
    AND f's `every named director filed consent and the section 146(1A) statements before incorporation`

-- s 20(1): "the Registrar must not register the constitution unless the Registrar is satisfied that all the requirements of
-- this Act in respect of the registration and of all matters precedent and incidental thereto have been complied with."
-- s 20(2): "the Registrar must refuse to register the constitution of a proposed company where the Registrar is satisfied that
-- -- (a) the proposed company is likely to be used for an unlawful purpose or for purposes prejudicial to public peace,
-- welfare or good order in Singapore; or (b) it would be contrary to the national security or interest ...".
-- s 19(3): "Upon receipt of the documents, information and payment ... and declaration ..., the Registrar must, subject to this
-- Act, register the company by registering its constitution."
-- READING: ss 145 and 146 are taken to be among "the requirements ... of all matters precedent" in s 20(1). s 146(1) is
-- expressly tied to "before ... the incorporation"; s 145(1) is a continuing rule that the encoding applies from the outset.
GIVEN f IS A Formation
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Registrar must register the constitution` f MEANS
        `section 19(1) is complied with` f
    AND `section 19(2) is complied with` f
    AND (NOT `section 17(5) bars registration` f)
    AND `the constitution meets section 22` f
    AND `the named directors meet sections 145 and 146` f
    AND (NOT f's `the Registrar is satisfied of a section 20(2) ground`)

-- s 18(1): "A company having a share capital may be incorporated as a private company if its constitution -- (a) restricts the
-- right to transfer its shares; and (b) limits to not more than 50 the number of its members ...".
-- s 4(1): "'public company' means a company other than a private company".
GIVEN f IS A Formation
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`it may be incorporated as a private company` f MEANS
        f's `it is to have a share capital`
    AND f's `the constitution restricts the right to transfer shares`
    AND f's `the constitution limits the members to not more than 50`

GIVEN f IS A Formation
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`it will be a public company` f MEANS NOT `it may be incorporated as a private company` f

§§ `171 -- the secretary`

-- s 171(1E): "Where a director is the sole director of a company, he or she must not act or be appointed as the secretary of the
-- company." s 171(3): the secretaries "are to be appointed by the directors". s 171(4A): "The office of secretary must not be left
-- vacant for more than 6 months at any one time."
GIVEN `the number of directors` IS A NUMBER, `the candidate is a director` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 171(1E) bars the candidate as secretary` `the number of directors` `the candidate is a director` MEANS
        `the number of directors` EQUALS 1
    AND `the candidate is a director`

GIVEN `months the office has been vacant` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the secretary's office has been vacant too long` `months the office has been vacant` MEANS
    `months the office has been vacant` GREATER THAN 6

§§ `157 -- the directors' general duty at every step`

-- s 157(1): "A director must at all times act honestly and use reasonable diligence in the discharge of the duties of his or her
-- office." (2): an officer or agent "must not make improper use of his or her position ... or any information acquired by virtue
-- of his or her position ... to gain, directly or indirectly, an advantage for himself or herself or for any other person or to
-- cause detriment to the company." (3): a breach makes the officer "(a) liable to the company for any profit made by him or her
-- or for any damage suffered by the company ... and (b) guilty of an offence and ... liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding
-- $20,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 12 months or to both." [Act 24 of 2025 wef 06/05/2026]
-- (4): "This section is in addition to and not in derogation of any other written law or rule of law" -- the general law of
-- directors' fiduciary duties survives beside it and is not encoded.
GIVEN `acted honestly` IS A BOOLEAN, `used reasonable diligence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the director is in breach of section 157(1)` `acted honestly` `used reasonable diligence` MEANS
    NOT (`acted honestly` AND `used reasonable diligence`)

GIVEN `made improper use of position or information` IS A BOOLEAN, `to gain an advantage or cause detriment to the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the officer is in breach of section 157(2)` `made improper use of position or information` `to gain an advantage or cause detriment to the company` MEANS
    `made improper use of position or information` AND `to gain an advantage or cause detriment to the company`

GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine under section 157(3), in dollars` MEANS 20000

GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment under section 157(3), in months` MEANS 12

§§ `161 -- the general meeting's approval before the directors issue shares`

-- s 161(1): "Despite anything in a company's constitution, the directors must not, without the prior approval of the company in
-- general meeting, exercise any power of the company to issue shares."
-- (3): the approval "continues in force until -- (a) the conclusion of the annual general meeting commencing next after the date
-- on which the approval was given; or (b) the expiration of the period within which the next annual general meeting after that
-- date is required by law to be held, whichever is the earlier; but any approval may be previously revoked or varied by the
-- company in general meeting."
-- Days are day numbers on any one scale. READING: the approval is taken to be in force on the day it is given (it is "prior"
-- to an issue later that day) and to be spent on the day the earlier of the two limits arrives.
GIVEN a IS A NUMBER, b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lesser of` a b MEANS
    IF a AT MOST b THEN a ELSE b

GIVEN `day of the issue` IS A NUMBER,
      `day the approval was given` IS A NUMBER,
      `day the next AGM concludes` IS A NUMBER,
      `last day by which the next AGM must be held` IS A NUMBER,
      `the approval was revoked before the issue` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the section 161 approval is in force on` `day of the issue` `day the approval was given` `day the next AGM concludes` `last day by which the next AGM must be held` `the approval was revoked before the issue` MEANS
        (NOT `the approval was revoked before the issue`)
    AND `day of the issue` AT LEAST `day the approval was given`
    AND `day of the issue` LESS THAN (`the lesser of` `day the next AGM concludes` `last day by which the next AGM must be held`)

-- s 161(4): "The directors may issue shares even though an approval ... has ceased to be in force if the shares are issued
-- pursuant to an offer, agreement or option made or granted by them while the approval was in force and they were authorised
-- by the approval to make or grant an offer, agreement or option which would or might require shares to be issued after the
-- expiration of the approval."
GIVEN `an approval is in force` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `issued under an offer made while an approval authorising it was in force` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the issue is authorised under section 161` `an approval is in force` `issued under an offer made while an approval authorising it was in force` MEANS
    `an approval is in force` OR `issued under an offer made while an approval authorising it was in force`

-- s 161(6): "Any issue of shares made by a company in contravention of this section is void and consideration given for the
-- shares is recoverable accordingly."
GIVEN `the issue is authorised` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the issue is void under section 161(6)` `the issue is authorised` MEANS NOT `the issue is authorised`

-- s 161(7): "Any director who knowingly contravenes, or permits or authorises the contravention of, this section ... shall be
-- liable to compensate the company and the person to whom the shares were issued ...; but no proceedings ... may be commenced
-- after the expiration of 2 years from the date of the issue." Months stand in for the two years; at exactly 24 the period has
-- not yet expired.
GIVEN `the issue is authorised` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the director knowingly contravened, permitted or authorised it` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `months from the issue to the proceedings` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`proceedings lie against the director under section 161(7)` `the issue is authorised` `the director knowingly contravened, permitted or authorised it` `months from the issue to the proceedings` MEANS
        (NOT `the issue is authorised`)
    AND `the director knowingly contravened, permitted or authorised it`
    AND `months from the issue to the proceedings` AT MOST 24

§§ `63 -- the private company's return of allotment`

-- s 63(1): "A private company may allot new shares, other than a deemed allotment, by lodging with the Registrar a return of the
-- allotment in the prescribed form" with the particulars in (a)-(e). (2): "An allotment of shares, other than a deemed
-- allotment, by a private company on or after 3 January 2016 does not take effect until the electronic register of members of
-- the company is updated by the Registrar under section 196A(5)." (3): "'deemed allotment' means an issue of shares without
-- formal allotment to subscribers to the constitution."
GIVEN `it is a deemed allotment to subscribers` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `a return of allotment was lodged` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the Registrar has updated the electronic register of members` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the private company's allotment has taken effect under section 63` `it is a deemed allotment to subscribers` `a return of allotment was lodged` `the Registrar has updated the electronic register of members` MEANS
        `it is a deemed allotment to subscribers`
    OR  (`a return of allotment was lodged` AND `the Registrar has updated the electronic register of members`)

GIVEN `shares held` IS A NUMBER, `shares in issue` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the percentage of the shares` `shares held` `shares in issue` MEANS
    `shares held` TIMES 100 DIVIDED BY `shares in issue`

§§ `79, 81-84 -- substantial shareholdings (Division 4 of Part 4)`

-- s 79(2): "A reference to a company is a reference -- (a) [Deleted by Act 2 of 2009] (b) to a body corporate, being a body
-- incorporated in Singapore, that is for the time being declared by the Minister, by notification in the Gazette, to be a
-- company for the purposes of this Division; or (c) to a body, not being a body corporate formed in Singapore, that is for the
-- time being declared by the Minister ...". So Division 4, s 81 included, reaches only a body the Minister has declared.
GIVEN `declared by the Minister for Division 4` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Division 4 reaches the company` `declared by the Minister for Division 4` MEANS `declared by the Minister for Division 4`

-- s 81(1): a person has a substantial shareholding if "(a) the person has an interest or interests in one or more voting shares
-- in the company; and (b) the total votes attached to that share, or those shares, is not less than 5% of the total votes
-- attached to all the voting shares in the company." (4): "voting shares" exclude treasury shares.
GIVEN `declared by the Minister for Division 4` IS A BOOLEAN, `percentage of the votes` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`has a substantial shareholding under section 81` `declared by the Minister for Division 4` `percentage of the votes` MEANS
        `Division 4 reaches the company` `declared by the Minister for Division 4`
    AND `percentage of the votes` AT LEAST 5

-- s 82(1): "A person who is a substantial shareholder in a company must give written notice to the company ...". (2)(b): "within
-- 2 business days after becoming a substantial shareholder". ss 83 and 84 likewise put the notice on the shareholder. None of
-- ss 82-84 is addressed to the directors.
DECLARE DutyHolder IS ONE OF
    `the substantial shareholder`
    `the directors`
    `the company`

GIVETH A DutyHolder
`who must give the section 82 notice` MEANS `the substantial shareholder`

GIVETH A NUMBER
`business days to give the section 82 notice` MEANS 2

-- s 83(3): "'percentage level' ... means the percentage figure ascertained by expressing the total votes attached to all the
-- voting shares in which the substantial shareholder has an interest ... as a percentage of the total votes attached to (a) all
-- the voting shares in the company ... and, if it is not a whole number, rounding that figure down to the next whole number."
-- (1): a notice is due "Where there is a change in the percentage level". s 84: a person who "ceases to be a substantial
-- shareholder" must notify within 2 business days.
GIVEN `percentage of the votes` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the section 83 percentage level` `percentage of the votes` MEANS FLOOR `percentage of the votes`

GIVEN `declared by the Minister for Division 4` IS A BOOLEAN, `percentage before` IS A NUMBER, `percentage after` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a section 83 notice is due` `declared by the Minister for Division 4` `percentage before` `percentage after` MEANS
        `has a substantial shareholding under section 81` `declared by the Minister for Division 4` `percentage before`
    AND `has a substantial shareholding under section 81` `declared by the Minister for Division 4` `percentage after`
    AND (NOT (`the section 83 percentage level` `percentage before` EQUALS `the section 83 percentage level` `percentage after`))

GIVEN `declared by the Minister for Division 4` IS A BOOLEAN, `percentage before` IS A NUMBER, `percentage after` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a section 84 notice is due` `declared by the Minister for Division 4` `percentage before` `percentage after` MEANS
        `has a substantial shareholding under section 81` `declared by the Minister for Division 4` `percentage before`
    AND (NOT `has a substantial shareholding under section 81` `declared by the Minister for Division 4` `percentage after`)

§§ `Part 11A and the Sixteenth Schedule -- the register of registrable controllers`

-- Sixteenth Schedule para 2(1): a person "has a significant interest in a company ... having a share capital -- (a) if [the
-- person] has an interest in more than 25% of the shares in the company ...; or (b) if -- (i) [the person] has an interest in one
-- or more voting shares ...; and (ii) the total votes attached to that share, or those shares, is more than 25% of the total
-- voting power in the company". Para 3, for a company without a share capital: a right "to share in more than 25% of the
-- capital, or more than 25% of the profits".
GIVEN `percentage of the shares held` IS A NUMBER, `percentage of the voting power held` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`has a significant interest under paragraph 2` `percentage of the shares held` `percentage of the voting power held` MEANS
        `percentage of the shares held` GREATER THAN 25
    OR  `percentage of the voting power held` GREATER THAN 25

GIVEN `percentage of the capital shared in` IS A NUMBER, `percentage of the profits shared in` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`has a significant interest under paragraph 3` `percentage of the capital shared in` `percentage of the profits shared in` MEANS
        `percentage of the capital shared in` GREATER THAN 25
    OR  `percentage of the profits shared in` GREATER THAN 25

-- Para 1: significant control if the person "(a) holds the right, directly or indirectly, to appoint or remove the directors ...
-- who hold a majority of the voting rights at meetings of the directors ...; (b) holds, directly or indirectly, more than 25% of
-- the rights to vote on those matters that are to be decided upon by a vote of the members ...; or (c) has the right to exercise,
-- or actually exercises, significant influence or control over the company".
GIVEN `can appoint or remove the directors with a majority of board votes` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `percentage of the members' votes held` IS A NUMBER,
      `exercises or may exercise significant influence or control` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`has significant control under paragraph 1` `can appoint or remove the directors with a majority of board votes` `percentage of the members' votes held` `exercises or may exercise significant influence or control` MEANS
        `can appoint or remove the directors with a majority of board votes`
    OR  `percentage of the members' votes held` GREATER THAN 25
    OR  `exercises or may exercise significant influence or control`

-- s 386AB: an "individual controller" or "corporate controller" is one "which has a significant interest in, or significant
-- control over, the company". s 386AC: a controller "is registrable unless" its interest or control "is only through one or
-- more controllers (B)" each of which itself keeps a register (or is otherwise listed in s 386AC(c)). s 386AA(1)(a): the Part
-- applies to "all companies other than a company that is set out in the Fourteenth Schedule".
GIVEN `has a significant interest` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `has significant control` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `holds only through controllers that themselves keep registers` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the company is set out in the Fourteenth Schedule` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the company must enter the person in its register of controllers` `has a significant interest` `has significant control` `holds only through controllers that themselves keep registers` `the company is set out in the Fourteenth Schedule` MEANS
        (NOT `the company is set out in the Fourteenth Schedule`)
    AND (`has a significant interest` OR `has significant control`)
    AND (NOT `holds only through controllers that themselves keep registers`)

-- s 386AF(1): a company incorporated on or after 31 March 2017 but before the appointed day "must keep a register of its
-- registrable controllers not later than 30 days after the date of the company's incorporation". (1A): a company incorporated
-- "on or after the appointed day must keep a register ... starting on the date of the company's incorporation". (14): the
-- appointed day is the commencement of s 4 of the Companies and Limited Liability Partnerships (Miscellaneous Amendments) Act
-- 2024. Companies incorporated before 31 March 2017 are not encoded.
GIVEN `incorporated on or after the appointed day` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`days after incorporation by which the register of controllers must be kept` `incorporated on or after the appointed day` MEANS
    IF `incorporated on or after the appointed day` THEN 0 ELSE 30

-- s 386AF(12): for failure to comply with (1), (1A), (2), (3), (7), (8), (9) or (11), "the company, and every officer of the
-- company who is in default, shall each be guilty of an offence and shall each be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding
-- $25,000."
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine under section 386AF(12), in dollars` MEANS 25000

§§ `76B, 76D, 76F, 184 -- a selective off-market buy-back`

DECLARE BuyBack HAS
    `the constitution expressly permits the company to acquire its own shares` IS A BOOLEAN
    `ordinary shares to be acquired in the relevant period` IS A NUMBER
    `ordinary shares in the class at the resolution date, treasury shares disregarded` IS A NUMBER
    `capital was reduced under section 78B, 78C or 78I in the relevant period` IS A BOOLEAN
    `votes for the special resolution` IS A NUMBER
    `votes against the special resolution` IS A NUMBER
    `days of written notice of the special resolution` IS A NUMBER
    `the seller or an associated person voted` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the shares are all the shares in their class` IS A BOOLEAN
    `percentage of the other holders of the class who consented` IS A NUMBER
    `the notice and resolution state an expiry no later than the next AGM` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the notice states the sources of funds and their impact` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the resolution is passed by written means under section 184A` IS A BOOLEAN
    `days the agreement was open for inspection at the registered office, ending with the meeting` IS A NUMBER
    `the agreement was available at the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 76B(1): "Despite section 76, a company may, in accordance with this section and sections 76C to 76G, purchase or otherwise
-- acquire shares issued by it if it is expressly permitted to do so by its constitution."
-- (3): "The total number of ordinary shares and stocks in any class that may be purchased or acquired by a company during the
-- relevant period must not exceed 20% ... of the total number of ordinary shares and stocks of the company in that class
-- ascertained as at the date of any resolution passed pursuant to section 76C, 76D, 76DA or 76E unless -- (a) the company has,
-- at any time during the relevant period, reduced its share capital by a special resolution under section 78B or 78C; or (b)
-- the Court has ... made an order under section 78I". (3E): treasury shares "disregarded".
GIVEN b IS A BuyBack
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the acquisition is within the section 76B(3) limit` b MEANS
        b's `capital was reduced under section 78B, 78C or 78I in the relevant period`
    OR  b's `ordinary shares to be acquired in the relevant period` TIMES 100
            AT MOST b's `ordinary shares in the class at the resolution date, treasury shares disregarded` TIMES 20

-- s 184(1): "A resolution is a special resolution when it has been passed by a majority of not less than three-fourths of such
-- members as, being entitled to do so, vote ... at a general meeting of which -- (a) in the case of a private company -- not less
-- than 14 days' written notice ... has been duly given." Votes counted are those of members entitled to vote; under s 76D(2) the
-- seller and the seller's associated persons are not among them, so their votes are not in the counts.
GIVEN b IS A BuyBack
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the special resolution passes in a private company` b MEANS
        b's `votes for the special resolution` GREATER THAN 0
    AND b's `votes for the special resolution` TIMES 4
            AT LEAST (b's `votes for the special resolution` PLUS b's `votes against the special resolution`) TIMES 3
    AND b's `days of written notice of the special resolution` AT LEAST 14

-- s 76D(2A) [Act 24 of 2025 wef 06/05/2026]: "Where the shares that are the subject of a selective off-market purchase ... belong
-- to a particular class of shares and do not constitute all the shares in that class, the company must, before passing the
-- special resolution ..., obtain the consent of at least 75% of the holders of the shares of that class (but excluding any person
-- whose shares are proposed to be purchased or acquired and the person's associated persons)". "75% of the holders" is read as
-- a count of holders; the text does not say whether it means holders by number or by shares held.
GIVEN b IS A BuyBack
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 76D(2A) class consent is satisfied` b MEANS
        b's `the shares are all the shares in their class`
    OR  b's `percentage of the other holders of the class who consented` AT LEAST 75

-- s 76D(3): the notice "must -- (a) specify a date on which the authority is to expire, being a date that must not be later than
-- the date on which the next annual general meeting ... is or is required by law to be held, whichever is the earlier; and (b)
-- specify the sources of funds to be used ... including the amount of financing and its impact on the company's financial
-- position." (4): "The special resolution ... must state the expiry date".
-- (7): the special resolution "is not effective ... unless ... a copy of the agreement or ... a written memorandum of its terms is
-- available for inspection by members ... both -- (a) at the company's registered office for not less than 15 days ending with
-- the date of the meeting ...; and (b) at the meeting itself." (4A)(b): if passed by written means under s 184A, "subsection (7)
-- does not apply" (the documents go to the voting members instead; not encoded).
GIVEN b IS A BuyBack
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 76D(7) inspection is satisfied` b MEANS
        b's `the resolution is passed by written means under section 184A`
    OR  (    b's `days the agreement was open for inspection at the registered office, ending with the meeting` AT LEAST 15
         AND b's `the agreement was available at the meeting`)

-- s 76D(2): "The terms of the agreement for a selective off-market purchase must be authorised by a special resolution of the
-- company, with no votes being cast by any person whose shares are proposed to be purchased or acquired or by the person's
-- associated persons".
GIVEN b IS A BuyBack
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the selective off-market purchase is authorised` b MEANS
        b's `the constitution expressly permits the company to acquire its own shares`
    AND `the acquisition is within the section 76B(3) limit` b
    AND `the special resolution passes in a private company` b
    AND (NOT b's `the seller or an associated person voted`)
    AND `section 76D(2A) class consent is satisfied` b
    AND b's `the notice and resolution state an expiry no later than the next AGM`
    AND b's `the notice states the sources of funds and their impact`
    AND `section 76D(7) inspection is satisfied` b

-- s 76F(4): "a company is solvent if at the date of the payment ... (a) there is no ground on which the company could be found to
-- be unable to pay its debts; (b) if -- (i) it is intended to commence winding up of the company within the period of 12 months
-- immediately after the date of the payment, the company will be able to pay its debts in full within the period of 12 months
-- after the date of commencement of the winding up; or (ii) it is not intended so to commence winding up, the company will be
-- able to pay its debts as they fall due during the period of 12 months immediately after the date of the payment; (c) the value
-- of the company's assets is not less than the value of its liabilities (including contingent liabilities) and will not, after
-- the proposed purchase ... become less than the value of its liabilities".
GIVEN `no ground to find it unable to pay its debts` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `winding up is intended within 12 months` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `able to pay in full within 12 months of the winding up` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `able to pay debts as they fall due for 12 months` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `assets not less than liabilities now` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `assets not less than liabilities after the purchase` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the company is solvent under section 76F(4)` `no ground to find it unable to pay its debts` `winding up is intended within 12 months` `able to pay in full within 12 months of the winding up` `able to pay debts as they fall due for 12 months` `assets not less than liabilities now` `assets not less than liabilities after the purchase` MEANS
        `no ground to find it unable to pay its debts`
    AND (IF `winding up is intended within 12 months`
         THEN `able to pay in full within 12 months of the winding up`
         ELSE `able to pay debts as they fall due for 12 months`)
    AND `assets not less than liabilities now`
    AND `assets not less than liabilities after the purchase`

-- s 76F(1): the payment "may be made out of the company's capital or profits so long as the company is solvent." (2)(a): if not,
-- "no purchase or acquisition by the company of its own shares pursuant to that agreement is lawful".
GIVEN `the purchase is authorised` IS A BOOLEAN, `the company is solvent at the date of payment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the buy-back is lawful` `the purchase is authorised` `the company is solvent at the date of payment` MEANS
    `the purchase is authorised` AND `the company is solvent at the date of payment`

-- s 76F(3): "Every director or chief executive officer of a company who approves or authorises, the purchase or acquisition of
-- the company's own shares ... knowing that the company is not solvent shall ... be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on
-- conviction to a fine not exceeding $100,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 3 years." No "or to both".
GIVEN `the director approved or authorised the purchase` IS A BOOLEAN, `the director knew the company was not solvent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the director commits the section 76F(3) offence` `the director approved or authorised the purchase` `the director knew the company was not solvent` MEANS
    `the director approved or authorised the purchase` AND `the director knew the company was not solvent`

GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine under section 76F(3), in dollars` MEANS 100000

GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment under section 76F(3), in months` MEANS 36

-- s 76B(5): ordinary shares bought "are, unless held in treasury in accordance with section 76H, deemed to be cancelled
-- immediately on purchase or acquisition." s 76B(7): "A private company may purchase or acquire any of its shares under section
-- 76C, 76D, 76DA or 76E by lodging the following with the Registrar: (a) a copy of a resolution ...; (b) a notice of purchase or
-- acquisition in the prescribed form". (8): the purchase "does not take effect until the electronic register of members of the
-- company is updated by the Registrar under section 196A(5)."
GIVEN `the shares are held in treasury` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the bought shares are cancelled under section 76B(5)` `the shares are held in treasury` MEANS NOT `the shares are held in treasury`

GIVEN `shares in issue before` IS A NUMBER, `shares bought and cancelled` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`shares in issue after the buy-back` `shares in issue before` `shares bought and cancelled` MEANS
    `shares in issue before` MINUS `shares bought and cancelled`

GIVEN `a copy of the resolution was lodged` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the notice of purchase was lodged` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the Registrar has updated the electronic register of members` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the private company's buy-back has taken effect` `a copy of the resolution was lodged` `the notice of purchase was lodged` `the Registrar has updated the electronic register of members` MEANS
        `a copy of the resolution was lodged`
    AND `the notice of purchase was lodged`
    AND `the Registrar has updated the electronic register of members`

§§ `17(5), 22, 38 -- the company limited by guarantee`

-- s 22(1)(c): each member "undertakes to contribute to the assets of the company, in the event of its being wound up while he or
-- she is a member or within one year after he or she ceases to be a member, for payment of the debts and liabilities of the company
-- contracted before he or she ceases to be a member and of the costs, charges and expenses of winding up ..., such amount as may be
-- required not exceeding a specified amount". Months stand in for the year. READING: for a member still in membership, "months
-- since ceasing" is 0 and every debt is "contracted before he or she ceases"; the costs of winding up are folded into the amount
-- required.
GIVEN `amount required` IS A NUMBER,
      `the specified amount` IS A NUMBER,
      `wound up while a member` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `months from ceasing to the winding up` IS A NUMBER,
      `the debts were contracted before the member ceased` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the guarantee contribution` `amount required` `the specified amount` `wound up while a member` `months from ceasing to the winding up` `the debts were contracted before the member ceased` MEANS
    IF     (`wound up while a member` OR `months from ceasing to the winding up` AT MOST 12)
       AND (`wound up while a member` OR `the debts were contracted before the member ceased`)
    THEN `the lesser of` `amount required` `the specified amount`
    ELSE 0

-- s 22(1AA): "Where a company to which subsection (1)(e) applies changes the number of its members with which it is registered,
-- the company must, within 14 days after the occurrence of such change, lodge with the Registrar a notice of the change in the
-- prescribed form." (1AB): "the company and every officer of the company who is in default ... liable on conviction to a fine not
-- exceeding $2,000 and also to a default penalty."
GIVETH A NUMBER
`days to notify a change in the registered number of members` MEANS 14

GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine under section 22(1AB), in dollars` MEANS 2000

-- s 38(1): "In the case of a company limited by guarantee, every provision in the constitution or in any resolution of the company
-- purporting to give any person a right to participate in the divisible profits of the company, otherwise than as a member, is
-- void."
GIVEN `the company is limited by guarantee` IS A BOOLEAN, `it gives a right to profits otherwise than as a member` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the provision is void under section 38(1)` `the company is limited by guarantee` `it gives a right to profits otherwise than as a member` MEANS
    `the company is limited by guarantee` AND `it gives a right to profits otherwise than as a member`
